Dear all,
We are pleased to announce two online courses in 2027 on the analysis of animal movement and habitat selection using R, designed for graduate students and researchers working with animal tracking and telemetry data.
 
1. Introduction to Analyzing Animal Movement with R - 1?3 March 2027
 [ https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/mve-r/ ]( https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/mve-r/ ) 
 
This introductory course provides practical training in processing and analyzing animal movement data in R. Topics include data management, identifying GPS outliers, calculating movement metrics, home-range analysis, and describing movement patterns using statistical distributions.
 
2. Analyzing Habitat Selection of Animals from Telemetry Data-  10?13 May 2027
[ https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/telemetry/ ]( https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/telemetry/ ) 
 
Building on the introductory course, this advanced training focuses on modeling habitat selection using telemetry data. Participants will learn to fit, interpret, and validate Resource Selection Functions (RSFs) and Step Selection Functions (SSFs), explore model extensions, and incorporate behavioral states using Hidden Markov Models.
 
Both courses are held online and combine lectures with practical coding sessions. Participants will receive example datasets and code, and are encouraged to bring their own data for hands-on exploration.
 
 
